# __Service__ node for n8n

This project defines an n8n node as typed action contracts with `@n8n/node-sdk`.
One action is one operation, e.g. `__service__.item.getAll`. n8n turns each action into a node type.
This file is the complete API reference. You do not have to read the SDK source.

## Layout

- `src/index.ts` exports `node`, `actions` (array) and `credentials` (array). Keep these names.
- `src/node.ts`: `defineNode`. `src/credentials.ts`: `defineCredential`.
- `src/actions/<resource>.<operation>.ts`: one `defineAction` for each file. Add each action to `actions`.
- `src/actions/<resource>.<operation>.test.ts`: unit tests with `node:test`, `runAction` and `mockHttp`.
- `src/actions/item.get-all.ts` and its test are an example: a list with `returnAll`, `limit` and cursor pages.
  Rename or replace them.

## Commands

```sh
n8n-node-next check                      # tsc --strict plus contract checks
n8n-node-next test                       # run src/**/*.test.ts; a test fails after 20 s
n8n-node-next describe [actionId]        # the typed module the AI builder sees
n8n-node-next run __service__.item.getAll --input '{"limit":5}' --credential-env __ENV__
```

`run` calls the live API and prints the items. `--credential-env __ENV__` reads the field `apiKey`
from `__ENV___API_KEY`. `--credential-file f.json` reads `{ "type": "...", "data": { ... } }`.
Run `check` and `test` after each change. Both must pass.

## Node and credential

```ts
defineNode({ id: '__service__', displayName: '__Service__', credentials: [__service__Api.name],
	baseUrl: 'https://api.example.com/v1' }); // add `authOptional: true` if the API also works without a key
defineCredential({
	name: '__service__Api', displayName: '__Service__ API',
	properties: [{ name: 'apiKey', displayName: 'API Key', type: 'string', typeOptions: { password: true }, required: true }],
	// A template is '={{$credentials.<field>}}'. Send it in a header, or in the query: { qs: { api_key: '=...' } }.
	authenticate: { headers: { 'X-Api-Key': '={{$credentials.apiKey}}' } },
	test: { request: { baseURL: 'https://api.example.com/v1', url: '/me' } },
});
```

## Action

```ts
defineAction({
	node,
	id: '__service__.item.create',          // <node>.<resource>.<operation>, unique
	action: 'Create an item',               // the label users pick
	summary: 'Create one item.',            // at most 120 characters
	flow: { effect: 'write', cardinality: 'per-item', passthrough: 'replace', idempotent: false },
	input: { name: str(), ownerId: str().optional() },
	output: item,
	async run({ input, http, emit }) {
		const body = { name: input.name, ...(input.ownerId ? { ownerId: input.ownerId } : {}) };
		const response = await http.request({ method: 'POST', path: '/items', body });
		emit(parse(item, response)); // throws e.g. "response.id: must be string"
	},
});
```

- `flow.effect`: `read` | `write` | `transform`. `flow.cardinality`: `per-item` (one call per input item),
  `1:N` (a list), `N:1`. `flow.passthrough`: `replace` (emit only `output`) | `merge`. `idempotent?: boolean`.
- `run()` runs once per input item. Call `emit(item)` once per output item. `emit` throws when the item
  does not match `output`. n8n pairs each item with its input item.
- In `run()`, a field with `.default(v)` is always set, also inside objects. Do not add `??` fallbacks.
  An `.optional()` field can be `undefined`.
- To fail an item, throw. Do not catch errors to emit `{ error }`: with "Continue on fail", n8n turns
  the thrown error into an `{ error: message }` item (or sends it to the error output) and runs the next item.
- `credentials?: string[]` on an action overrides the node's credential types.
- When the output shape depends on an input, declare all shapes and pick one in `deriveOutput`:
  `output: union(invoice, line)`, `deriveOutput: (input) => (input.split ? line.json : invoice.json)`.
- Never read credentials in `run()`. The credential applies to each request.

## Schemas

| Builder | TypeScript type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `str()` `num()` `int()` `bool()` | `string` `number` `number` `boolean` | `int` allows integers only |
| `oneOf('a', 'b')` | `'a' \| 'b'` | a fixed list of options |
| `lit('a')` | `'a'` | one fixed value |
| `nullable(s)` | `T \| null` | for output fields the API sets to `null` |
| `arr(s)` | `readonly T[]` | |
| `obj({ k: s })` | `{ k: T }` | rejects unlisted fields |
| `record(s)` | `Record<string, T>` | any keys, checked values |
| `json()` | `Record<string, unknown>` | any object, not checked |
| `variant('mode', { a: {...}, b: {...} })` | tagged union | fields that depend on a choice |
| `union(a, b)` | `A \| B` | a value that matches one of the schemas |

- Chain `.optional()`, `.default(v)` (also optional for callers), `.hint(text)` (at most 80 characters),
  `.describe(text)`, `.with({ pattern, minimum, maximum, minLength, format, examples })`.
- `obj` rejects fields it does not list. To emit an API object unchanged, list all of its fields,
  or keep unlisted fields with `obj({ ... }).with({ additionalProperties: true })`.
- Every `examples` value must match its schema. Do not make a field conditionally required: use `variant`.
- `variant('kind', { text: { text: str() }, json: { data: json() } })` is
  `{ kind: 'text'; text: string } | { kind: 'json'; data: Record<string, unknown> }`. A branch `{}` has only the tag.
  Narrow it in `run()` with `if (input.body.kind === 'text') input.body.text`, or a `switch` on the tag.
- `parse(schema, value)` returns the typed value or throws with each failing path. `matches(schema, value)`
  is a type guard. `Infer<typeof schema>` is the TypeScript type. `isRecord(v)` and `list(v)` narrow `unknown`.

## HTTP

- `http.request({ method, path, url, query, headers, body, fullResponse, timeoutMs, retry })`. Give `path`
  (starts with `/`, goes after `baseUrl`) or `url` (absolute, e.g. a `next` link), not both.
  A `query` value that is `undefined` is not sent; an array repeats the key (`id=a&id=b`). `body` is sent as JSON. It returns the parsed JSON body
  as `unknown`: narrow it with `parse`. `timeoutMs` is 300000 when omitted.
- `fullResponse: true` returns `{ body, headers, statusCode }` as `unknown`. Header names are lower case:
  `const full = obj({ body: arr(item), headers: json() }).with({ additionalProperties: true });`
  `if (!matches(full, response)) throw ...;` then `response.body` is typed; check `typeof response.headers.link`.
- A non-2xx response throws. After `isHttpError(error)`, read `error.status`, `error.body` and
  `error.headers` (lower case, e.g. `error.headers['retry-after']`).
- Do not write retries. n8n retries a 429, 502, 503, 504 or a dropped connection up to 3 times, with
  backoff and `Retry-After`, for GET, HEAD, PUT, and every request of an action with `flow.idempotent: true`.
  `retry: true` also retries another method; `retry: false` never retries.
- Paging: `paginate(http, { request(cursor, room), items(body), next(body), limit?, maxPages? })` yields
  the items; see `src/actions/item.get-all.ts`. Do not write a page loop. One run may send 10000 requests.

## Tests

```ts
const fetch = mockHttp([
	{ method: 'POST', path: '/items', reply: { status: 201, json: { id: 'itm_1', name: 'A', ownerId: null } } },
]);
const result = await runAction(createItem, { input: { name: 'A' }, credential, credentials, fetch });
assert.deepEqual(result, { ok: true, items: [{ id: 'itm_1', name: 'A', ownerId: null }] });
assert.deepEqual(fetch.calls[0]?.body, { name: 'A' });
```

- `runAction(action, { input, credential, credentials, fetch })` runs the action through the executor
  n8n uses: it fills in defaults, validates the input, retries, and validates each item. An input value
  `''` counts as unset, as in n8n. It returns `{ ok: true, items }` or
  `{ ok: false, error: { message, path?, httpStatus? } }`. It does not throw.
- A route matches on `method` (default `GET`), the end of the URL path, and each listed `query` parameter
  (other parameters may also be present). When more routes match, the route with the most listed query
  parameters answers. `times: n` answers at most n calls, then the next matching route answers.
- `reply`: `{ status?, json?, headers? }`. A call that no route matches fails with the list of routes.
- `fetch.calls[i]`: `{ method, url, path, query, headers, body }`. Query values are strings (a repeated
  key is an array), header names are lower case, a JSON body is already parsed.
- Compare the whole result with `assert.deepEqual(result, ...)`: a failure then shows `result.error`.
- A run with more than 1000 mock calls fails: the code loops over the same page.
